      "problem": "Write the equation of the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}=60$ in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $60$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2} & =60 \\\\ \\frac{5{y}^{2}}{60}-\\frac{12{x}^{2}}{60} & =\\frac{60}{60} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
